{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn (call|run-exception-program|compose-exception|publish-donor)|backends|def frontends' test/yang/call/conformance.clj; sed -n '1,130p' test/yang/call/conformance.clj; rg -n ':test|:kondo|antlr|cljstyle' deps.edn; rg -n 'Portable try|finally' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | tail -12; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*kondo*' -g '*cljstyle*'; git diff 96633aaf...854b74c3 --stat; ls target\"","aggregated_output":"112:(def frontends\n207:(defn publish-donor!\n306:          (keys h/backends))))\n317:(defn call\n337:(defn compose-exception\n465:  (into (sorted-map) (map (fn [backend] [backend e]) (keys h/backends))))\n468:(defn run-exception-program\n488:                     (keys h/backends))]\n(ns yang.call.conformance\n  \"The cross-language calling gates' shared composition (docs/design/\n   yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11): a donor program's named export reaches a\n   caller program by explicit published-export composition only.\n\n   A donor is real source of any admitted frontend, lowered unmodified and\n   published as an ordinary linker module whose one export, `body`, is the\n   lowered unit. A caller task requires that module, runs its body under the\n   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`, `py/run-main`,\n   `clj/run-main`), reads each named export from the donor runtime's global\n   namespace, and projects it into the caller runtime's namespace under the\n   same name; then the caller source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own\n   entry. The composition is a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is\n   rewritten, no foreign `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is\n   inserted, and the projected value is the donor's own callable value\n   (identity survives).\n\n   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\n   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\n   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\n   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\n\n   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\n   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\n   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php`, `py` and `clj` are\n   published beside them. The AST walker is not a backend: its links are\n   refused until L-b.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yang.clojure :as clj-comp]\n    [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\n    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n    [yang.core.names :as names]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as py-lower]\n    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as py-parser]\n    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as py-prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.render :as py-render]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(defn- publish-guest!\n  \"Publish guest module `spec` into the harness store, throwing immediately\n   with `result` in ex-data if publication is refused.\"\n  [spec]\n  (let [result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n    (when (= :refused (:status result))\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"Guest module publication refused: \" (or (:reason result) (:status result)))\n                      result)))\n    result))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-php\n  \"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\n   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\"\n  (delay (publish-guest!\n           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-py\n  \"`py` published beside `js` and `php`, over the same host registry and\n   `yang.call` revision.\"\n  (delay (publish-guest!\n           (py-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                   (:call-address @h/published)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-clj\n  \"`clj` published beside `js`, `php` and `py`, over the same host registry\n   and `yang.call` revision.\"\n  (delay (publish-guest!\n           (clj-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n\n\n(defn- parse-ok\n  \"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\"\n  [parse source]\n  (let [pk (parse source)]\n    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\n      (throw (ex-info \"donor or caller source does not parse\"\n                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\n    pk))\n\n\n(defn- python-export-symbol\n  [export]\n  (symbol (str \"xlang.python.export.\" export)))\n\n\n(defn- python-unit\n  [packet exports]\n  (u/lam [py-lower/globals-sym py-lower/globals-fn-sym]\n         (u/seq-nodes\n           (concat (map (fn [export]\n                          (u/sexp->uast\n                            (list 'py/global-set py-lower/globals-sym\n                                  {:py/str export} (python-export-symbol export))))\n                        exports)\n                   [(py-lower/lower-module-body packet)]))))\n\n\n(def frontends\n  \"Each admitted frontend's profile, as data:\n\n   - `:runtime`, `:address`: the runtime module and its published address;\n   - `:refusal`: the publication refusal key and reason of its modules;\n   - `:deps` (optional): pinned requirements beyond the runtime its\n     lowered units read directly (the clojure unit's `yang.call` reads);\n   - `:parse`: source text to CST packet;\n   - `:unit`: packet and projected exports to the lowered unit its\n     `:run-main` entry takes;\n   - `:read-export`: export name to the form reading the runtime's global\n     namespace (JS `globalThis`, PHP's named-function table, Python's main\n     module dictionary, the clojure runtime's task-local namespace cell);\n   - `:project`: name and a value form to the form binding the value where\n     the runtime's source resolves a called name;\n   - `:render`: the `:run-main` value as test data.\"\n  {:typescript\n   {:runtime 'js,\n    :address #(:address @h/published),\n12:        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n13:        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n14:        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n20: ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n21: ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n23:         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\" \"build/antlr/php/classes\"\n24:         \"build/antlr/typescript/classes\"]\n31:           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n59:           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\" \"build/antlr/php/js\"]\n115:           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n116:           :antlr-gen {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n117:                       :extra-deps {org.antlr/antlr4 {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}}\n118:                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yang-antlr-gen\"]}\n119:           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n149:;; clj -M:test\n150:;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n151:;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n152:;; clj -M:test -n yin.repl.python-antlr-test\n153:;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n154:;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n1126:          try (let [clauses (filter #(and (seq? %) (#{'catch 'finally} (first %))) ops)\n1127:                    body (take-while #(not (and (seq? %) (#{'catch 'finally} (first %)))) ops)\n1136:                  (reject! \"Portable try requires one Exception/ExceptionInfo catch and no finally\"\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_kondo.txt\n.cljstyle\nAGENTS.md\ncollab/yin-ucf/logs/d15-kondo1.log\ncollab/yin-ucf/logs/d15-kondo2.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-kondo.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/ld1-kondo-comparison.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/5c-cljstyle.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/ld1-kondo.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-r3-cljstyle-final.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-kondo-final.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-r3-kondo.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-r3-cljstyle.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-r4-cljstyle.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/ld1-kondo-baseline.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/5c-r2-cljstyle.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-r4-kondo.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-cljstyle-final.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/5c-r2-kondo.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-r4-cljstyle-final.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/5c-kondo.log\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/6a-r3-kondo-final.log\ncollab/yang-python/1790875893000-compiler-engineer-python-c2-s1.orchestrator-cljstyle.log\ncollab/yang-python/1790875893000-compiler-engineer-python-c2-s1.orchestrator-kondo.log\ncollab/yin-vm/6cpre-kondo.log\ncollab/yin-vm/1790187551464-compiler-engineer-debruijn-cljstyle-linelen.prompt.md\ncollab/yin-vm/1791910000000-5a-r2-cljstyle.log\ncollab/yin-vm/1791910000000-5a-r2-kondo.log\ncollab/yin-vm/1791850000000-5a-kondo.log\ncollab/yin-vm/p5b-r2-kondo.log\ncollab/yin-vm/1791850000000-5a-cljstyle-final.log\ncollab/yin-vm/1791850000000-5a-kondo-final.log\ncollab/yin-vm/p5b-r2-cljstyle.log\ncollab/yin-vm/1790187551464-compiler-engineer-debruijn-cljstyle-linelen.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\ncollab/yin-vm/6cpre-r2-kondo.log\ncollab/yin-vm/1791850000000-5a-cljstyle.log\n src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc                         | 1290 +++++++++-----------\n src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc                 |   76 +-\n 